    "hoa_name": "Palm Hibiscus Star Islands Association, Inc.",
    "cdd_name": null,
    "is_gated": true,
    "geo_point": null,
    "notes": "Star Island is a small, exclusive man-made residential island in Biscayne Bay, completed in 1922 by the Army Corps of Engineers. Located within the City of Miami Beach, it features approximately 30-35 single-family waterfront estates and a fixed supply of ~35 lots. Per Bloomberg, it is the most expensive neighborhood in the United States. The island is part of the Biscayne Bay Aquatic Preserve and is accessible via the MacArthur Causeway. It lies south of the Venetian Islands and just east of Palm and Hibiscus Islands. Total area is 0.134 sq mi (0.35 km²), ZIP 33139."
  },
